## Frequently asked questions

### What is an SEO reseller?

An SEO reseller is an agency or freelancer that sells SEO services to its own clients and buys the delivery from a specialist. The reseller sets the client price and manages the relationship. The supplier does the work under the reseller's brand.

### How do I choose the best SEO reseller partner?

Ask who will actually do the work, whether deliverables are bespoke or templated, and whether non-solicitation is in writing. Ask for a sample deliverable in your branding. Check that the supplier makes no ranking guarantees. No one controls Google's results.

### Will you sign an NDA?

Yes. I'm happy to work under an NDA covering your agency, your clients and your pricing.

### Will my clients ever know you are involved?

Only if you choose to tell them. Reports and documents arrive unbranded or in your template. I join any client call you invite me to as part of your team.

### Do you offer local SEO reseller services?

Yes. I deliver Google Business Profile work, location pages, citations, review processes and local reporting under your brand. Scope is agreed per client.

### Do you guarantee rankings or AI citations?

No. Rankings depend on competition, links, content and how Google assesses the site. AI answers change between runs. I agree measurable work and report honestly on what changed.

### How do I start as a reseller partner?

Book a partner call through the contact page. Bring one client site and a rough idea of what you want to sell. The first project is usually an audit. It gives both of us a clear picture of the work.

